CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ deduced pack arity through partial-spec base: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG must FAIL: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
A class template partial specialization whose parameter pack follows fixed
(non-deduced) template arguments, selected via the partial-specialization
disambiguation path (as a dependent base class), must deduce the pack to all
trailing arguments rather than collapsing it to one element.  This is the shape
of libstdc++'s __result_of_impl<false,false,_Functor,_ArgTypes...> behind
multi-argument std::function.  N5008 [temp.spec.partial.match], [temp.variadic]/5.

Fixed in cpp_typecheck_resolvet::disambiguate_template_classes: after
build_template_args (which emits a single scalar convenience binding for the
pack), expand the deduced pack into one positional argument per element via
pack_args_map, mirroring elaborate_class_template, so the specialization is
instantiated with the pack bound to all trailing arguments and sizeof...(A) is
correct.  Non-vacuous (assertion 2 must FAIL).
